This directory contains code for the LSTM pipeline 

installing the packages:
1. create a venv by running:
    "python -m venv <venv_name>"
2. activate the venv:
    "source bin/<venv_name> activate"
3. download the packages:
    pip install -r requirements.txt

Running the code:

    python src/compute_metrics.py <dir_containing_results_of_experiment> <dir_to_save_metrics_to>

    computes the metrics for the results of all households and saves it to files, the metrics stored are MAE, RMSE, and MAPE

    python src/make_error_distribution_graphs.py <dir_containing_results_of_experiment> <dir_to_save_plots_to>
    python src/make_error_distribution_graphs_aggregate.py <dir_containing_results_of_experiment> <dir_to_save_plots_to>
    
    both plot error distribution graphs

    python src/make_weekday_error_distribution_graphs.py <dir_containing_results_of_experiment> <dir_to_save_plots_to>
    python src/make_weekday_error_distribution_graphs_aggregate.py <dir_containing_results_of_experiment> <dir_to_save_plots_to>

    similar to the the previous two but weekday error distribution graphs

    python src/make_result_plots.py <dir_containing_results_of_experiment> <dir_to_save_plots_to>
    python src/make_result_plots_aggregate.py <dir_containing_results_of_experiment> <dir_to_save_plots_to>

    This will plot the results compared to the true values for every day in the results

